    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0714" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.579/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-24">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 7</hi>.] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 594]</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that I have received from His Majesty’s Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs
                    copies of lists of articles, the exportation of which the kingdoms of <pb
                        facs="0715" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/> Norway, Sweden, and Denmark have
                    prohibited under agreement with the British Government, and I beg to enclose
                    herewith these copies in duplicate.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d609-f1"/> In this
                    connection I further have the honor to inform the Department of the fact that
                    these lists form an integral part of the program as to contraband which has been
                    adopted, by His Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Nines Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d609-f1" n="1" xml:id="d609-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; of considerable length. They resemble in general the Dutch list
                    summarized ante, <ref target="#pg388">p. 388</ref>. See also the Ambassador’s
                    telegrams Nos. 1202, December 6, and 1209, December 7, regarding the inclusion
                    of copper in the Swedish list, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg356">pp. 356</ref>, <ref target="#pg359">359</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
